cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data, or figures, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "RepFix: Spectral Toxicity Filtering for Multi-Task Representation Learning"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation, per-seed result files, and run logs for the paper
  "Gradient Toxicity: When Auxiliary Heads Collapse the Shared Encoder".  The
  repository contains the training and evaluation code, the per-table
  configuration files and seed lists, and the raw per-seed results from which
  every number reported in the paper can be recomputed.
type: software
authors:
